+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create, pay and cancel orders, and administrators can create coupons, but there is
+no way to actually redeem a coupon. Orders always charge the full amount (`discountCents = 0`),
+so the coupon data model (`discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`,
+`coupon_redemptions`, `used_count`) is currently unused. Customers expect to apply one coupon to a
+pending order and see the payable amount drop before they pay.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "..." }`.
+- Validate the request body and the order state, then look up the coupon by its normalized
+  (trimmed, upper-cased) code.
+- Enforce coupon eligibility: active status, validity window against the injected clock, per-order
+  single-use, and global usage limit.
+- Compute the discount for FIXED and PERCENT coupons, applying the coupon cap and never going below
+  a zero payable amount.
+- Persist the result atomically: update the order's `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents` and
+  `coupon_code`, insert one `coupon_redemptions` row, and increment `coupons.used_count` in a
+  single transaction.
+- Return the updated order (response identical to `GET /orders/:id`); never change the order status.
+- Add tests for the new behavior. No schema change, no new dependency.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupon`: applying a coupon to a pending order and the resulting payable amount, redemption
+  record, and usage accounting.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- None: there is no existing spec under openspec/specs/ yet. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- New route `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`.
+- Business rules in `src/services/orderService.ts` (or a dedicated redemption service) using the
+  injected `Clock`.
+- SQL for the atomic update in `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` and
+  `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts`; a single transaction is orchestrated at the repository
+  layer.
+- Uses existing tables only: `orders`, `coupons`, `coupon_redemptions` (no migration).
+- New tests in `tests/`; no changes to existing tests or benchmark tests.
